This is very helpful. Now I understand the mechanism:

- `_scan_graph_index_health` computes `lag_h = (search_index.mtime - graphml.mtime)/3600`. If lag > max_lag_h (48h), it either:
  - if last self-heal was < 6h ago → issue = "陈旧...6h内已试自愈未恢复——升级人工"
  - else → call `_graph_index_selfheal(lag_h, max_lag_h)` and set state["graph_index_heal_last"]=now. If ok → issue=None (graphml advanced, next beat naturally re-checks recovery). If not ok → issue = "陈旧...自动增量重建失败: note".

- The `_scan_infra_liveness` etc. are called every probe beat.

- The infra_alerts are written to gate-blocked.log and message to wangyuyan only when there are NEW infra_alerts (via idempotency: `state["graph_index_issue"]` only reports when issue changed).

